From f020af235a94c45b789a75d22b13931235052198 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt C <latentcollapse@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:54:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 32/45] np2: resume a reply cut off at the output limit instead
 of ending the run

A NeuraJL trial run stopped mid-task after a threshold compaction. The
trace shows the cause was the reply before it: cut off at the output token
limit (stopReason length) with no tool call, which the agent loop took as
the model finishing. Compaction then ran on an assistant-last turn and,
with no goal, the run ended. Compactions in the middle of a tool loop
already resumed correctly (now covered by tests).

A truncated reply now queues one resume prompt, at most three in a row, on
both the natural-stop path and the threshold-compaction path, which skips
the continuation hook. An active goal keeps priority.

Tests: one and repeated compactions, compaction with a stateful tool's
post-compaction note, tool calls after compaction, the user's request run
exactly once, truncation with and without compaction, the three-in-a-row
bound, and no continuation after a normal stop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
